## Data and Security Rules

Preserve the following data behavior:

- Every user has a private profile.
- Profiles are stored in Firebase under the authenticated user ID.
- Categories belong to one authenticated user.
- Notes belong to a category and its authenticated owner.
- Users must only see their own categories.
- Users must only see their own notes.
- Users must not read, update, or delete another user’s data.
- Category names and note text must not be empty.
- Trim whitespace before saving text.
- Never expose another user’s private data in the UI.

